section.para:
			Annotate a document, read the layer, then produce a redacted copy in which
			only detected spans are replaced. Length is preserved: every character
			inside a mention becomes the mask character, and everything outside stays
			unchanged. PiiUsageExampleTest asserts the behavior shown
			here.

String text =
    "Contact jane@example.com, call (555) 123-4567, or charge card 4111 1111 1111 1111.";

Document document = new PiiAnnotator(new CursorPiiExtractor())
    .annotate(Document.of(text));

List<Annotation<PiiMention>> mentions = document.get(PiiAnnotator.PII);
// email, phone, card: exact spans, types, and normalized forms

String masked = Masker.mask(document, PiiAnnotator.PII, '*');
// "Contact ****************, call **************, or charge card *******************."

			CompositePiiExtractor runs several extractors over one text
			and merges the result, and PiiPacks names the combinations
			worth having: payment(), contact(),
			network(), secrets(), crypto(),
			usIdentity(), euIdentity(),
			caIdentity(), device(), and
			allStructured() for everything. Overlaps are resolved the way
			a single extractor resolves them: the leftmost candidate wins, then the
			longest, then the more specific type, so a value two types both claim
			resolves the same way whichever pack was listed first.

String text = "Deploy from 10.0.0.7 using AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE, ask jane@example.com.";

List<PiiMention> mentions = PiiPacks.allStructured().extract(text);
// ipv4, aws-access-key, email

PiiExtractor keysOnly = PiiPacks.secrets();
PiiExtractor custom = new CompositePiiExtractor(
    new CursorPiiExtractor(), new NetworkPiiExtractor());

			Masking hides a value but also destroys the fact that two mentions were
			the same value, which is what makes a redacted support ticket unreadable.
			Pseudonymizer replaces each mention with a numbered label
			instead, giving the same value the same label throughout the text. Labels
			are rarely as long as what they replace, so the returned
			PiiRewrite carries the new text together with a mapping for
			moving other annotations onto it.

String text = "Contact jane@example.com; jane@example.com replied to bob@example.com.";

PiiRewrite rewrite = new Pseudonymizer()
    .rewrite(text, new CursorPiiExtractor().extract(text));
// "Contact EMAIL-1; EMAIL-1 replied to EMAIL-2."

int moved = rewrite.mapOffset(text.indexOf("bob@example.com"));
List<Annotation<String>> tokens = rewrite.remap(originalTokens);

PiiAuditReport is what a review can be given instead of the mentions: how many of each type, how many were distinct, and a keyed token per distinct value rather than the value. Nothing in a report carries a value or an offset, but its tokens remain linkable pseudonymous data.
PiiAuditReport report = PiiAuditReport.of(document, tokenizer);
report.total(); // 3 report.counts().get(PiiMention.TYPE_CARD); // 1 report.distinctCounts(); // repeats counted once report.samples(PiiMention.TYPE_EMAIL); // tokens, never addresses
